# THE CHECKOUT LINE-ENDING INVARIANT
#
#     A FinancialStandards checkout must not let the cloning machine's `core.autocrlf` decide the
#     bytes of tracked text files. Repository-declared attributes determine checkout line endings,
#     with explicit exceptions only where this repository has evidence they are required.
#
# WHAT THIS FIXES, MEASURED. Before this file existed, a fresh worktree that no editor had touched
# materialised 201 of 201 tracked files as CRLF while every committed blob was LF. Nothing in the
# repository said what the bytes should be, so each machine decided.
#
# THIS IS NOT A FORMATTING PREFERENCE. `test/init.test.mjs:220` compares templates/AGENTS.md against
# templates/CLAUDE.md after stripping HTML comments with `/<!--[\s\S]*?-->\n*/`. Under CRLF the `\n*`
# never matches — the next byte is `\r` — so the two files differ by the newlines the regex failed to
# consume, and the test FAILED on every Windows checkout and inside the CI container, which is built
# by COPYing the working tree. It passes on a Linux checkout. That is the whole failure mode: a
# defect that only appears where the machine translated, invisible to a hosted Linux run.
#
# NO EXCEPTIONS ARE DECLARED, AND THAT IS DELIBERATE. Each was tested against this repository's own
# evidence rather than inherited from a sibling:
#
#   * No tracked file is binary. `text=auto` detects that itself, so no `-text` rule is needed; the
#     measurement found zero tracked files git treats as non-text.
#   * `*.ps1` (scripts/ci.ps1, scripts/submit-pr.ps1) get LF like everything else. PowerShell reads
#     LF, and no evidence was found that either file requires CRLF.
#   * `artifacts/**/retrieved.sha256` digests cover `retrieved.md` files that each directory's own
#     .gitignore excludes from tracking. Attributes apply to tracked content, so this declaration
#     cannot move those digests. test/checkout-line-endings.test.mjs pins that.
#
# Adding an exception later means adding it to NOT_LF_BY_DECLARATION in
# test/checkout-line-endings.test.mjs too, with the evidence. The two are read together.
#
# THIS DOES NOT REWRITE A CHECKOUT THAT ALREADY EXISTS. Refresh one with:
#     git rm --cached -r . && git reset --hard
#
# It is also not a history renormalisation, and must not become one: every blob here is already LF.
# The defect is in what lands on disk, never in what was stored.
* text=auto eol=lf
